      "review_title": "",
      "review_description": "The sales person did not try to sell me the most expensive unit but listened to my requirements and recommended a system to fit. With FIT at only 6c you must try and use as much of what you generate as you can so as to reduce your pay back time. I installed a 2kW system using Rene Solar Panels, not the most expensive but fitted to my situation with a 3kW Power One Aurora Inverter.Always pay for a top line inverter and allow for any future expansion.My system is North facing on 25 degree roof and starts up not more than 45 minutes after sun up with maximum power around 1950 kW. I expect to be saving around $200 per quarter.When looking at solar you need to chart out your power usage against time of day, if most of your power is used early morning and late at night it might not be worth it.",
